  "label": "`label` is the human name for a class and the only string a console or CLI should print to a person; `class` is the identifier and the only string that travels on the wire. `architecture` groups a vendor generation for display and is never placed against.",
  "devices_per_node": "Devices sharing one coherent interconnect, which is the unit a replica is laid out in: tensor parallelism stays inside it and pipeline parallelism crosses it over the backend fabric. Absent means the default of 8, an HGX board. Present where the part is sold as a rack-scale domain \u2014 a GB300 NVL72 is 72 devices and one node, however many chassis of silicon that is. A cluster's own `supply_topology_domain.device_count` overrides this."
